---
notes: |
  Appended to the editor's user prompt for a suggested rewrite, on the hosted
  path (convex/agents.ts suggestRewrite) and the bring-your-own-key path
  (src/utils/ai-client.ts runClientRewrite), so both ask for the same thing.
  {sizeRule} is the sentence/paragraph length rule; {original} is the passage.
  The fact rule exists because evals caught rewrites that "simplified" a term
  of art away or dropped the place a claim was about.
version: "2"
---

REWRITE TASK: Rewrite the PASSAGE below in your voice, preserving its meaning but doing the work better. {sizeRule}

Keep every name, number, date, place and term of art the passage contains unless the rewrite's purpose is to correct one; the writer's facts are not yours to drop. If a technical term is the problem, keep the term and explain it in plain words rather than replacing it.

Respond as JSON only, no prose: {"replacement": "<rewritten passage as plain text>", "rationale": "<one sentence, in your voice>"}

PASSAGE:
"{original}"
---
notes: |
  Citation-format system prompt — turns messy/incomplete citations into
  clean bibliographic entries.
version: "1"
---

You are a meticulous research librarian. Your only job is to take a messy, informal, or incomplete citation and return a clean, properly formatted bibliographic entry. Extract all available fields (title, author, year, URL, DOI, publisher). If information is missing, leave that field blank. Respond as JSON only.
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* ── Selection actions ────────────────────────────────────────────
   A small piece of editorial furniture attached to the selected passage.
   It keeps research, marginalia, and persona requests in the manuscript. */
.selection-actions {
  position: fixed;
  z-index: var(--z-dropdown);
  width: max-content;
  max-width: min(32rem, calc(100vw - 1rem));
  border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink-muted) 52%, transparent);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-paper) 91%, transparent);
  box-shadow: 0 0.65rem 1.8rem rgba(32, 25, 16, 0.2);
  backdrop-filter: blur(14px) saturate(0.9);
  color: var(--color-ink);
}
.selection-actions--above {
  transform: translate(-50%, -100%);
}
.selection-actions--below {
  transform: translateX(-50%);
}
.selection-actions__row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: stretch;
}
/* On a phone the row wraps rather than clipping its last actions. */
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .selection-actions__row {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
}
.selection-actions__row > button {
  padding: 0.5rem 0.58rem;
  border-right: 1px solid
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-paper-3) 72%, transparent);
  color: var(--color-ink-light);
  font-family: var(--font-typewriter);
  font-size: 0.7rem;
  letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
.selection-actions__row > button:hover:not(:disabled) {
  color: var(--color-vermilion);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-vermilion) 6%, transparent);
}
.selection-actions__row > button:disabled {
  cursor: wait;
  opacity: 0.45;
}
.selection-actions__row > .selection-actions__close {
  border-right: 0;
  color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  font-size: 0.8rem;
}
.selection-actions__error {
  padding: 0.4rem 0.55rem;
  border-top: 1px solid
    color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-vermilion) 30%, transparent);
  color: var(--color-vermilion);
